IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa08-types`

-- Pensions Act 2008 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: WORKPLACE PENSION STATUS, AND
-- QUALIFYING EARNINGS AND CONTRIBUTIONS (ss 1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 20).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2008-30.txt.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — status, earnings and contributions`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- ss 3(6B), 13(2): "In the case of a pay reference period of less or more
-- than 12 months, subsection (1) applies as if the amount[s] ... were
-- proportionately less or more."
@ref ss 3(6B), 13(2)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, p IS A `Pay reference period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount` amount `pro rata for` p MEANS
    amount TIMES (p's `length in months` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- s 13(1) "A person's qualifying earnings in a pay reference period of 12
-- months are the part (if any) of the gross earnings payable to that person
-- in that period that is— (a) more than £6,240, and (b) not more than
-- £50,270."
@ref s 13(1)-(2)
@export The qualifying earnings in a pay reference period under s 13 of the Pensions Act 2008 (UK): the part of the gross earnings above £6,240 and not above £50,270, both scaled to the length of the period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`  @desc The length of the period in months and the gross earnings in it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the qualifying earnings in` p MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (    `the lesser of` (p's `gross earnings`) (`the amount` 50270 `pro rata for` p)
       MINUS `the amount` 6240 `pro rata for` p)

-- Ages on day d: "aged at least 16" from the 16th birthday; "under 75"
-- before the 75th; "aged at least 22" from the 22nd.
GIVEN w IS A `Worker facts`, n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker` w `is aged at least` n `on` d IF
    d AT LEAST `add years` (w's `date of birth`) n

DECLARE `Pension status` IS ONE OF
    `to be automatically enrolled`
    `a jobholder who may opt in`
    `a worker who may ask to join under s 9`
    `not within the duties`

-- s 1(1) a jobholder "(a) ... is working or ordinarily works in Great
-- Britain under the worker's contract, (b) ... is aged at least 16 and under
-- 75, and (c) to whom qualifying earnings are payable". s 3(1): automatic
-- enrolment for a jobholder "(a) who is aged at least 22, (b) who has not
-- reached pensionable age, and (c) to whom earnings of more than £10,000 are
-- payable" (pro rata, (6B)). s 7: other jobholders not in a qualifying
-- scheme may opt in. s 9: a worker within (a) and (b) but not (c) may ask to
-- join a s 9 scheme.
@ref ss 1(1), 3(1)-(4), (6B), 7(1)-(2), 9(1)
@export The workplace pension status of a worker in a pay reference period under the Pensions Act 2008 (UK), judged on the period's first day: to be automatically enrolled (a jobholder aged 22 to pensionable age earning more than £10,000 pro rata, s 3); or, where s 3(3)-(4) disapplies that, as any other jobholder; a jobholder who may opt in (s 7); a worker without qualifying earnings who may ask to join (s 9); or not within the duties. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN w IS A `Worker facts`         @desc Date of birth, pensionable age, working in Great Britain, and scheme membership
      p IS A `Pay reference period` @desc The period's first day, length and gross earnings
GIVETH A `Pension status`
`the pension status of` w `in` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT inScope THEN `not within the duties`
        IF `the qualifying earnings in` p EQUALS 0 THEN
            IF w's `an active member of a section 9 scheme` THEN `not within the duties` ELSE `a worker who may ask to join under s 9`
        -- s 3(3)-(4) disapply only s 3(2); the jobholder then falls to s 7
        -- like any other (changed after the independent pass, L146, L150).
        IF eligible AND NOT (w's `excepted from automatic enrolment by s 3(3) or (4)`) THEN `to be automatically enrolled`
        IF w's `an active member of a qualifying scheme` THEN `not within the duties`
        OTHERWISE `a jobholder who may opt in`
    WHERE
        d MEANS p's `first day`
        inScope MEANS
                w's `works or ordinarily works in Great Britain under the worker's contract`
            AND `the worker` w `is aged at least` 16 `on` d
            AND NOT (`the worker` w `is aged at least` 75 `on` d)
        eligible MEANS
                `the worker` w `is aged at least` 22 `on` d
            AND d LESS THAN w's `reaches pensionable age on`
            AND p's `gross earnings` GREATER THAN `the amount` 10000 `pro rata for` p

-- s 20(1) "(b) the employer's contribution ... must be equal to or more than
-- 3% of the amount of the jobholder's qualifying earnings ...; (c) the total
-- amount of contributions paid by the jobholder and the employer ... must be
-- equal to or more than 8%". (1A): for a relevant Master Trust, also
-- Conditions 1 and 2.
@ref s 20(1)-(1A)
@export Whether a UK money purchase scheme meets the quality requirement in s 20 of the Pensions Act 2008 (UK) for a jobholder in a pay reference period: the employer pays at least 3% and the employer and jobholder together at least 8% of the qualifying earnings (and, for a relevant Master Trust, Conditions 1 and 2 are met). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`  @desc The period and its earnings
      c IS A `Contributions`         @desc The employer's and the jobholder's contributions, and the Master Trust conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contributions meet the quality requirement in` p `with` c IF
        c's `employer contribution` GREATER THAN 0
    AND c's `employer contribution` AT LEAST 0.03 TIMES qe
    AND c's `employer contribution` PLUS c's `jobholder contribution` AT LEAST 0.08 TIMES qe
    AND c's `Master Trust conditions met or not a Master Trust`
    WHERE
        qe MEANS `the qualifying earnings in` p
